+# Whispers in the Court 0.8.5 — NoDebug EN1
+
+An English edition of the player's RU NoDebug fork, prepared for review by the
+original author. The original mod, MIT license and author credits are retained.
+The player's RU build remains separate and is not modified by preparing this package.
+
+## Run the English edition
+
+1. Close EU5 and any existing Court Brain window. Keep a separate save before trying
+   another mod edition; a fresh disposable campaign is best for the first check.
+2. Run `WhispersInTheCourt-0.8.5-NoDebug-EN1.exe` and choose **Open Court Brain**.
+3. Configure your own AI provider. This edition starts with fresh settings: it does
+   not import the RU player's keys, ChatGPT sign-in, instructions or campaign memory.
+4. Use **Install mod** while EU5 is closed. Enable **WIC NoDebug 0.8.5 EN** in the
+   launcher and disable every other Whispers in the Court edition.
+5. Set EU5 to English for the English in-game interface. Start through Steam normally,
+   with neither `-debug_mode` nor `-console` in the launch options. Leave Court Brain
+   open while playing. The companion UI and default AI output language are English.
+
+The original provider options, Russian support and the experimental ChatGPT option
+are retained. No provider account is needed for the no-AI diagnostic below. Providers
+require the player's own access; normal AI requests use their service's allowance.
+
+## Independent paths
+
+- Settings/account storage: `%LOCALAPPDATA%/WhispersInTheCourt-NoDebug085-EN/`.
+- Mod: `Documents/Paradox Interactive/Europa Universalis V/mod/WhispersInTheCourtNoDebug085EN/`.
+- Campaign memory/log: `Documents/Paradox Interactive/Europa Universalis V/court_brain_nodebug085_en/`.
+- Poll file: `Documents/Paradox Interactive/Europa Universalis V/run/votc_nd85en_poll.txt`.
+
+These are separate from the RU 0.8.5 paths. Only one companion/edition should run at
+a time. To return to RU, close the game and EN companion, select the RU mod and run
+its previous EXE with the appropriate saved game. EN memory is not merged back.
+
+## Reproduce the transport without AI
+
+Choose **Test events without AI** in the startup window:
+
+1. Close the game and install the EN1 build from that diagnostic window.
+2. Start a disposable English campaign with only this edition enabled and no debug flags.
+3. Send long text. Check spaces, quotes, punctuation, paragraphs and the final
+   **END OF LONG TEXT: everything arrived.** Close the event.
+4. Replace it with short text. Check that no tail of the long message remains.
+5. Show the test law and open the socio-economic laws window. Check **Grain Charter**,
+   both options and their English descriptions. There is no need to enact it to check
+   the text. It occupies custom law slot 1, so do not run this step in a valued campaign.
+6. Tick only what you actually observed and save the diagnostic report.
+
+The report records the received ACKs, debug/achievement flags and visual confirmations.
+It does not claim a Steam achievement unlock. Test an ordinary achievement separately
+if reproducing that result. The RU player has already reported one actual Steam unlock;
+the newly packaged EN1 itself has not yet had a live campaign test.
+
+## Build from source on Windows x64
+
+Use Python with tkinter and SSL (the source requires Python 3.10 or newer). In the
+source folder, create a virtual environment, activate it, then run:
+
+```powershell
+python -m pip install -r tools/court_brain/requirements.txt
+python -m pip install pyinstaller
+python -m unittest discover -s tools -p "test_*.py" -q
+python tools/validate_mod.py
+python tools/build_exe.py
+```
+
+The generated static localization and pinned librakaly DLL are already included.
+Regenerating text expressions is optional: `python tools/gen_nodbg_text.py`. Preserve
+the manifest's existing IDs. The build copies the original icon and mod into a single
+EXE; users do not need Python installed separately.
+
+Optional packaged checks (supply an absolute report path):
+
+```powershell
+.\dist\WhispersInTheCourt-0.8.5-NoDebug-EN1.exe --verify-build C:\Temp\wic-build.json
+.\dist\WhispersInTheCourt-0.8.5-NoDebug-EN1.exe --verify-https C:\Temp\wic-https.json
+```
+
+The first is offline and uses a scratch mailbox. The second contacts a public Google
+HTTPS endpoint without a key or inference request; an HTTP error such as 404 is an
+expected valid TLS response. Neither installs the mod or changes real campaign data.
+
+## Review material
+
+Read `docs/NODEBUG-TECHNICAL-NOTES.md` for the mechanism, file map, evidence and limits.
+`README-UPSTREAM.md` preserves the original author's instructions as historical
+reference; its debug-mode advice does not describe this edition. The older RU readme
+is likewise retained as history, not EN1 setup instructions. The handoff package also
+contains a text diff, source archive, test summary, licenses and the supplied achievement
+screenshot. No user configuration, API keys, authentication cache, saves or gameplay
+logs are distributed.
