+Hi! I've been playing Whispers in the Court and working on a Russian adaptation with help from OpenAI Codex. We got a version working without `-debug_mode`, and I've now actually unlocked a Steam achievement while playing with the RU NoDebug mod enabled.
+
+The key finding was that GUI-triggered console execution, `run` and `console_history.txt` still worked with debug mode off in my tested EU5 build (1.3.11). We kept that bridge, but replaced runtime localization reloads with preloaded localization expressions that render text stored in global variables. Punctuation, spaces and long responses are preserved, and an acknowledgement of the text stamp is required before the event and its effects are sent. We also added read-only binary save conversion for normal-mode saves.
+
+I've tested decrees, autonomous events, choices and actual gameplay effects in the RU versions. I also noticed fewer freezes and crashes, although that is an observation rather than a benchmark.
+
+I prepared a separate English build, full source, a diff against your 0.8.5 release, technical notes and an achievement screenshot for you to review. The English package passes local tests and executable checks; it still needs its own live in-game test. The achievement was earned with the RU build.
+
+The package contains no personal keys or saves. It includes some unrelated localization and experimental ChatGPT work, which the notes identify separately from the NoDebug changes. I'd be happy for you to review the approach and bring any useful parts into the main mod. Thanks for creating it — it has made my campaigns much more interesting!
